  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "A card is drawn at random from a pack of 52 playing cards. It is replaced and the pack is shuffled. A second card is then drawn. What is the probability of the event:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "both cards are Diamonds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{16}$",
          "worked": "Replacement makes the draws independent.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{both Diamonds})&=\\frac{13}{52}\\times\\frac{13}{52}\\\\P(\\text{both Diamonds})&=\\frac{1}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "neither card is a Diamond?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{9}{16}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{neither Diamond})&=\\frac{39}{52}\\times\\frac{39}{52}\\\\P(\\text{neither Diamond})&=\\frac{9}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "only one of the cards is a Diamond?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{8}$\n\nAdd the probabilities of the two possible orders.",
          "worked": "The Diamond can be first or second; these cases are mutually exclusive.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly one Diamond})&=\\frac{13}{52}\\times\\frac{39}{52}+\\frac{39}{52}\\times\\frac{13}{52}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one Diamond})&=\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{3}{16}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one Diamond})&=\\frac{3}{8}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "only the first card is a Diamond?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{16}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{only first Diamond})&=\\frac{13}{52}\\times\\frac{39}{52}\\\\P(\\text{only first Diamond})&=\\frac{3}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "only the second card is a Diamond?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{16}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{only second Diamond})&=\\frac{39}{52}\\times\\frac{13}{52}\\\\P(\\text{only second Diamond})&=\\frac{3}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "at least one of the cards is a Diamond?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{16}$\n\nSubtract the probability of neither card being a Diamond from 1.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one Diamond})&=1-P(\\text{neither Diamond})\\\\P(\\text{at least one Diamond})&=1-\\frac{39}{52}\\times\\frac{39}{52}\\\\P(\\text{at least one Diamond})&=\\frac{7}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
